IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`
IMPORT `spr-nouns`
IMPORT `spr-part3-deferral`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PART 7: regulations 21 to 23 (overseas residents).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
--
-- Not among the inputs, so taken as plain inputs below:
--   * "overseas resident" (a term of the 2014 Act, not defined in these Regulations);
--   * whether regulations have been made applying regulation 21 to a given up-rating
--     increase (regulation 21(2)): the freeze on up-rating works only if such regulations
--     exist, so that fact gates the whole of regulation 21 (fork F25);
--   * the weekly rates in regulation 22 and the percentage of section 17(4).
-- "At the time of that increase" (21(4)) and "immediately before the up-rating
-- increase comes into force" (21(5)) are taken as the same moment (fork F23).

§ `Part 7: Overseas Residents`

§§ `Regulation 21(6): the specified territory`

-- Gloss: any part of the Channel Islands that is not covered by an Order under section
-- 179 of the Administration Act (which makes reciprocal arrangements) is a "territory
-- specified" for sections 18(4) and 20(2) and (3) of the 2014 Act.
-- src:295 | (6) For the purposes of sections 18(4) and 20(2) and (3) of the 2014 Act, the territory specified is any part of the Channel Islands which is not subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act.
@ref Regulation 21(6) (src:295)
GIVEN `the place is in the Channel Islands` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 21(6): the place is a territory specified for sections 18(4) and 20(2) and (3) of the 2014 Act` `the place is in the Channel Islands` `the place is subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act` MEANS
    `the place is in the Channel Islands` AND NOT (`the place is subject to an Order made under section 179 of the Administration Act`)

§§ `Regulation 21: entitlement to up-rating increases`

DECLARE OverseasFacts HAS
    `regulations have been made providing that regulation 21 applies to this up-rating increase` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the up-rating increase comes into force` IS A DATE
    `the period of deferral, if the person's entitlement was ever deferred` IS A MAYBE DeferralPeriod
    `when the deferral period ended the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `when the deferral period ended the person was an overseas resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act immediately before the increase comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an overseas resident at the time the increase comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person continued to be an overseas resident until the deferral period ended` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE UpratingOutcome IS ONE OF
    `the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase under regulation 21`
    `regulation 21 does not take the up-rating increase away`
    `regulation 21 does not apply to this up-rating increase`

-- Gloss, paragraph (3): paragraph (4) is for a person whose entitlement was deferred for
-- a period and who, when the deferral ended, was entitled to a state pension and was an
-- overseas resident.
-- src:282 | (3) Paragraph (4) applies in a case where—
-- src:283 | (a) a person’s entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act has been deferred for a period; and
-- src:284 | (b) when the deferral period ends, that person is—
-- src:285 | (i) entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act; and
-- src:286 | (ii) an overseas resident.
@ref Regulation 21(3) (src:282-286)
GIVEN facts IS A OverseasFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 21(3): paragraph (4) applies` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the period of deferral, if the person's entitlement was ever deferred`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST deferral THEN
            facts's `when the deferral period ended the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act`
        AND facts's `when the deferral period ended the person was an overseas resident`

-- Gloss, paragraph (4): for such a person, no up-rating increase (a) in respect of the
-- deferral period, if they were overseas when it happened and stayed overseas until the
-- deferral ended; or (b) after the deferral ended, if they are overseas when it happens.
-- An increase "in respect of the deferral period" is read as one that comes into force
-- during it (fork F26).
-- src:287 | (4) Where this paragraph applies, the person mentioned in paragraph (3) is not entitled to any up-rating increases—
-- src:288 | (a) in respect of the deferral period if—
-- src:289 | (i) the person was an overseas resident at the time of that increase; and
-- src:290 | (ii) the person continued to be an overseas resident until the deferral period ended; and
-- src:291 | (b) after the deferral period ended if the person is an overseas resident at the time of that increase.
@ref Regulation 21(4) (src:287-291)
GIVEN facts IS A OverseasFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 21(4): the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the period of deferral, if the person's entitlement was ever deferred`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST deferral THEN
        IF       facts's `the date the up-rating increase comes into force` AT LEAST deferral's `first day of the deferral`
             AND facts's `the date the up-rating increase comes into force` AT MOST deferral's `last day of the deferral`
        THEN     facts's `the person is an overseas resident at the time the increase comes into force`
             AND facts's `the person continued to be an overseas resident until the deferral period ended`
        ELSE IF facts's `the date the up-rating increase comes into force` GREATER THAN deferral's `last day of the deferral`
             THEN facts's `the person is an overseas resident at the time the increase comes into force`
             ELSE FALSE

-- Gloss, paragraph (5): in all other cases, no increase for a person who was entitled to
-- a state pension and an overseas resident immediately before the increase.
-- src:292 | (5) In all other cases, a person is not entitled to up-rating increases where, immediately before the up-rating increase comes into force, they were—
-- src:293 | (a) entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act; and
-- src:294 | (b) an overseas resident.
@ref Regulation 21(5) (src:292-294)
GIVEN facts IS A OverseasFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 21(5): the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person is entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act immediately before the increase comes into force`
    AND facts's `the person is an overseas resident at the time the increase comes into force`

-- Paragraph (2) makes regulation 21 apply to an up-rating increase only if regulations
-- have been made saying so. Paragraph (1) is the rule that those regulations switch on.
-- src:276 | (1) An overseas resident who is entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is not entitled to up-rating increases in accordance with this regulation.
-- src:277 | (2) This regulation—
-- src:278 | (a) applies in relation to an up-rating increase if Regulations are made—
-- src:279 | (i) in consequence of an order under section 150A (annual up-rating) or 151A of the Administration Act or in consequence of any other legislation; and
-- src:280 | (ii) which provide that this regulation applies to that up-rating increase; and
-- src:281 | (b) is subject to the Regulations made as mentioned in sub-paragraph (a).
@ref Regulation 21(1) and (2) (src:276-281)
GIVEN facts IS A OverseasFacts
GIVETH A UpratingOutcome
`regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` facts MEANS
    IF NOT (facts's `regulations have been made providing that regulation 21 applies to this up-rating increase`)
    THEN `regulation 21 does not apply to this up-rating increase`
    ELSE IF (IF `regulation 21(3): paragraph (4) applies` facts
             THEN `regulation 21(4): the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase` facts
             ELSE `regulation 21(5): the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase` facts)
         THEN `the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase under regulation 21`
         ELSE `regulation 21 does not take the up-rating increase away`

§§ `Regulation 22: modification of the increment for an overseas resident`

DECLARE PartOfDeferral HAS
    `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE ReferenceRate IS ONE OF
    `the weekly rate immediately before the start of that part of the deferral period`
    `the weekly rate immediately before the end of that part of the deferral period`
    `regulation 22 gives no reference rate for this part`

-- Gloss, paragraph (1): regulation 22 matters if the person was an overseas resident
-- for any part of the deferral period.
-- src:297 | (1) Subject to regulation 23, this regulation applies in cases where, during any part of the deferral period, a person has been an overseas resident.
@ref Regulation 22(1) (src:297)
GIVEN parts IS A LIST OF PartOfDeferral
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 22(1): regulation 22 applies` parts MEANS
    any (GIVEN part YIELD part's `the person was an overseas resident during the part`) parts

-- Gloss, paragraphs (2) and (3): for a part of the deferral period when the person was an
-- overseas resident and not in Great Britain or a specified territory, the increment is
-- worked on the weekly rate just before the START of that part; for a part when they were
-- not an overseas resident, on the weekly rate just before the END of that part.
-- A part when they were an overseas resident but in Great Britain or a specified territory
-- is in neither paragraph: nothing is said (fork F27).
-- src:298 | (2) For any part of the deferral period during which the person was an overseas resident and was not in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6), section 17(4) of the 2014 Act is modified to provide that the amount of an increment is equal to a percentage specified in regulations of the weekly rate of the state pension to which the person would have been entitled immediately before the start of that part of the deferral period if the person’s entitlement had not been deferred.
-- src:299 | (3) For any part of the deferral period during which the person was not an overseas resident, section 17(4) of the 2014 Act is modified to provide that the amount of an increment is equal to a specified percentage of the weekly rate of the state pension to which the person would have been entitled immediately before the end of that part of the deferral period if the person’s entitlement had not been deferred.
@ref Regulation 22(2) and (3) (src:298-299)
GIVEN part IS A PartOfDeferral
GIVETH A ReferenceRate
`regulation 22(2) and (3): the rate on which the increment for the part is worked` part MEANS
    IF part's `the person was an overseas resident during the part`
    THEN IF part's `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part`
         THEN `regulation 22 gives no reference rate for this part`
         ELSE `the weekly rate immediately before the start of that part of the deferral period`
    ELSE `the weekly rate immediately before the end of that part of the deferral period`

-- The increment for a part: the specified percentage of regulation 10, times the whole
-- weeks counted for that part (how the weeks are shared among the parts is not said,
-- fork F16), times the reference rate the paragraphs choose. NOTHING where regulation 22
-- gives no reference rate.
@ref Regulation 22(2) and (3) (src:298-299)
GIVEN part IS A PartOfDeferral
      `the whole weeks counted in the part` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 22: the increment for the part` part `the whole weeks counted in the part` `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part` `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulation 22(2) and (3): the rate on which the increment for the part is worked` part
    WHEN `the weekly rate immediately before the start of that part of the deferral period` THEN
        JUST (`regulation 10: the specified percentage for section 17(4) of the 2014 Act` TIMES `the whole weeks counted in the part` TIMES `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part`)
    WHEN `the weekly rate immediately before the end of that part of the deferral period` THEN
        JUST (`regulation 10: the specified percentage for section 17(4) of the 2014 Act` TIMES `the whole weeks counted in the part` TIMES `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part`)
    WHEN `regulation 22 gives no reference rate for this part` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 23: where regulations 12A and 22 both apply`

-- Gloss, paragraph (1): both apply at the same time when the weekly rate changed
-- (regulation 12A) and the person was overseas for some part (regulation 22(1)).
-- src:301 | (1) This regulation applies in a case where section 17(4) of the 2014 Act falls to be modified under both regulations 12A and 22 at the same time.
@ref Regulation 23(1) (src:301)
GIVEN deferral IS A DeferralPeriod
      `the dates of the non-uprating changes` IS A LIST OF DATE
      parts IS A LIST OF PartOfDeferral
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 23(1): regulations 12A and 22 both apply` deferral `the dates of the non-uprating changes` parts MEANS
        `regulation 12A(1): regulation 12A applies` deferral `the dates of the non-uprating changes`
    AND `regulation 22(1): regulation 22 applies` parts

-- Gloss, paragraph (4): when regulation 12A is applied on top of regulation 22, the
-- "weekly rate" regulation 12A(2) names is the one regulation 22(2) or 22(3) gives for
-- the part concerned.
-- src:304 | (4) The amount of the increment is then determined in accordance with the modifications set out in regulation 12A as if the reference in regulation 12A(2) to the weekly rate of the state pension were a reference to the weekly rate referred to in—
-- src:305 | (a) regulation 22(2), for any part of the deferral period during which the person was an overseas resident and was not in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6); and
-- src:306 | (b) regulation 22(3), for any part of the deferral period during which the person was not an overseas resident.
@ref Regulation 23(4) (src:304-306)
GIVEN part IS A PartOfDeferral
GIVETH A ReferenceRate
`regulation 23(4): the rate that stands in place of the weekly rate in regulation 12A(2)` part MEANS
    `regulation 22(2) and (3): the rate on which the increment for the part is worked` part

-- Gloss, paragraphs (3) and (5): first work out the increment under regulation 22; then
-- work it out under regulation 12A with the rate of paragraph (4); then add the increase
-- (or subtract the decrease) that results to the first amount.
-- The text does not say what the "increase or decrease" is measured against (fork F24);
-- it is taken as the difference that regulation 12A makes, supplied as an input, positive
-- for an increase and negative for a decrease.
-- src:303 | (3) The amount of the increment is first determined in accordance with the modifications set out in regulation 22.
-- src:307 | (5) Any increase or decrease of the increment as determined in accordance with paragraph (4) is then added to, or subtracted from, the amount of the increment as determined in accordance with paragraph (3).
@ref Regulation 23(3) and (5) (src:303) (src:307)
GIVEN `the increment determined in accordance with regulation 22` IS A NUMBER
      `the increase (positive) or decrease (negative) determined in accordance with paragraph (4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 23(5): the increment where regulations 12A and 22 both apply` `the increment determined in accordance with regulation 22` `the increase (positive) or decrease (negative) determined in accordance with paragraph (4)` MEANS
    `the increment determined in accordance with regulation 22` PLUS `the increase (positive) or decrease (negative) determined in accordance with paragraph (4)`
